{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790285966,"nonce":"+ZICzJ+Lft0esKwgItnZGNfPAr8=","title":"CI Windows: the checkout converts text files to CRLF","message":"GitHub's Windows runners have `core.autocrlf=true`, and the repository has no `.gitattributes`, so actions/checkout writes every text file with CRLF line endings. The Python and Lua conformance suites compare the frontends' stdout (which writes `\\n`) byte for byte against pinned `.expected` files, so every case would read as a failure there; the programs themselves, the grammars (`ml.zyn`) and the stdlib sources are also read as CRLF on Windows only.\n\nThe Windows job has never reached those suites (it stopped at compile errors, the build-script stack overflow, or the bench_memory_probe hang), so this is not yet observed in a log.\n\nFix: `.gitattributes` with `* text=auto eol=lf`. Every tracked text file is already LF in the index (`git ls-files --eol`), so renormalizing changes no content.","files":null}]}